{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Also at that time.</b> With a luminous countenance, so that His name not be profaned, for I prayed lest the inhabitants of the land say, 'HaShem brought us out from there from inability of HaShem to bring them' etc. But after you cross the Jordan and He kills thirty-one kings before you and gives you the land as an inheritance — if you sin against Him, prayer will not avail you, for there will be no profanation to say 'from inability of HaShem to bring them' etc. Rather, all the nations will say, 'Why did HaShem do so?' and they will say, 'Because they forsook' etc., and HaShem uprooted them from upon their land." "<b>As the first days.</b> Forty days and forty nights — from dawn of the twenty-ninth of Av until dawn of the tenth of Tishrei."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:20.737040782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}